00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:41.540
there was not very much time between uh, the end of season three

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:43.000
and the beginning of season four,

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:44.740
we had to come up with ideas really quickly.

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:47.660
Um, and I was sitting around with my brothers during Christmas

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:48.660
and we were reminiscing,

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:52.160
and lamenting the fact that how we were so poor in our twenties,

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:56.080
and, uh, didn't know -realize how poor we were being raised by a single mom,

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:58.420
and I wanted to take it back to those sort of

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:01.880
Spielbergy and type uh, struggles you see in like, uh

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:05.000
E.T. where the kids and the single mom were really poor

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:07.520
and they had to have their human struggles, and for us,

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:10.760
in the writer's room it was a way to get back to um,

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:14.060
human problems, as opposed to creating or inventing

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:18.220
another really complicated mythology based around a supernatural creature.

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:22.440
So we have assassins and -and bad guys this year who are a little more human,

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:25.360
